14069	"An anthranilic acid derivative with analgesic, anti-inflammatory, and antipyretic properties. It is used in musculoskeletal and joint disorders and administered by mouth and topically. (From Martindale, The Extra Pharmacopoeia, 30th ed, p16)"	""	""	""	""	""	"Flufenamic acid is a solid."	"Flufenamic acid is anatomically related to musculo-skeletal system."	"Flufenamic acid is in the therapeutic group of antiinflammatory and antirheumatic products."	"Flufenamic acid is pharmacologically related to antiinflammatory and antirheumatic products, non-steroids."	"The chemical and functional group of  is fenamates."	"Flufenamic acid is part of Acids, Carbocyclic ; Amines ; Aminobenzoates ; Aniline Compounds ; Anti-Inflammatory Agents ; Antiinflammatory and Antirheumatic Products ; Antiinflammatory and Antirheumatic Products, Non-Steroids ; Benzene Derivatives ; Benzoates ; Fenamates ; Musculo-Skeletal System ; OAT1/SLC22A6 inhibitors ; ortho-Aminobenzoates."	"Flufenamic acid is approved."	""	"The molecular weight is 281.23."	"Flufenamic acid has a topological polar surface area of 49.33."	"The log p value of  is 5.38."
