15312	"A methylxanthine derivative that inhibits phosphodiesterase and affects blood rheology. It improves blood flow by increasing erythrocyte and leukocyte flexibility. It also inhibits platelet aggregation. Pentoxifylline modulates immunologic activity by stimulating cytokine production. "	"The half-life is 0.4-0.8 hours"	"For the treatment of patients with intermittent lameness or immobility arising from chronic occlusive arterial disease of the limbs."	"Pentoxifylline inhibits erythrocyte phosphodiesterase, resulting in an increase in erythrocyte cAMP activity. Subsequently, the erythrocyte membrane becomes more resistant to deformity. Along with erythrocyte activity, pentoxifylline also decreases blood viscosity by reducing plasma fibrinogen concentrations and increasing fibrinolytic activity. It is also a non selective adenosine receptor antagonist."	"70%"	"Pentoxifylline, a synthetic dimethylxanthine derivative structurally related to theophylline and caffeine, is used in the treatment of peripheral vascular diseases and in the management of cerebrovascular insufficiency, sickle cell disease, and diabetic neuropathy."	"Pentoxifylline is a solid."	"Pentoxifylline is anatomically related to cardiovascular system and respiratory system."	"Pentoxifylline is in the therapeutic group of peripheral vasodilators and drugs for obstructive airway diseases."	"Pentoxifylline is pharmacologically related to peripheral vasodilators and other systemic drugs for obstructive airway diseases."	"The chemical and functional group of  is purine derivatives and xanthines."	"Pentoxifylline is part of Alkaloids ; Antioxidants ; Antiplatelet agents ; Blood Viscosity Reducer ; Cardiovascular Agents ; Compounds used in a research, industrial, or household setting ; Cytochrome P-450 CYP1A2 Substrates ; Cytochrome P-450 Substrates ; Drugs for Obstructive Airway Diseases ; Drugs that are Mainly Renally Excreted ; Enzyme Inhibitors ; Free Radical Scavengers ; Hematologic Activity Alterati