15830	"1,2-Dichlorobenzene, also named ortho-dichlorobenzene, is an organic compound. It is a non-polar colorless liquid that is miscible in most organic solvents. This derivative of benzene differs from the parent compound by the presence of two adjacent chlorine atoms. 1,2-dichlorobenzene is used as a precursor for agrochemicals, as a solvent for fullerenes, as an insecticide and as an agent to remove carbon-based contamination from metal."	""	""	""	""	""	"1,2-dichlorobenzene is a solid."	""	""	""	""	"1,2-dichlorobenzene is part of Agrochemicals ; Benzene Derivatives ; Compounds used in a research, industrial, or household setting ; Cytochrome P-450 CYP2E1 Substrates ; Cytochrome P-450 Substrates ; Hydrocarbons, Chlorinated ; Hydrocarbons, Halogenated ; Insecticides ; Pesticides ; Toxic Actions."	"1,2-dichlorobenzene is experimental."	""	""	""	""
