16051	"SPI-1620 is an endothelin B receptor agonist. In animal models SPI-1620 selectively and transiently increases tumor blood flow allowing increased delivery of anticancer agents to the tumor. It is being developed as an adjunct to chemotherapy."	""	"Investigated for use/treatment in cancer/tumors (unspecified)."	"SPI-1620 is a highly selective peptide agonist of endothelin-B receptors, which can stimulate receptors on endothelial cells, the innermost layer of cells lining the blood vessels. The blood supply to tumors is different than the blood supply to healthy organs. Blood vessels in the growing part of tumors are relatively devoid of smooth muscle covering and are rich in endothelial cells. Therefore, by stimulating the endothelial-B receptors present on the endothelial cells, SPI-1620 should selectively increase tumor blood flow while sparing healthy tissue."	""	"In animal models SPI-1620 selectively and transiently increases tumor blood flow allowing increased delivery of anticancer agents to the tumor."	"IRL-1620 is a solid."	""	""	""	""	"IRL-1620 is part of Amino Acids, Peptides, and Proteins ; Biological Factors ; Intercellular Signaling Peptides and Proteins ; Peptides ; Proteins."	"IRL-1620 is investigational."	""	""	""	""
