18687	"Cilastatin is an inhibitor of renal dehydropeptidase, an enzyme responsible for both the metabolism of thienamycin beta-lactam antibiotics as well as conversion of leukotriene D4 to leukotriene E4. Since the antibiotic, , is one such antibiotic that is hydrolyzed by dehydropeptidase, cilastatin is used in combination with imipenem to prevent its metabolism. The first combination product containing both drugs was approved by the FDA in November of 1985 under the trade name Primaxin, marketed by Merck & Co. A newer triple-drug product was approved in July 2019 under the trade name Recarbrio which also contains."	"The half-life of cilastatin is approximately 1h."	"Cilastatin is indicated, in combination with with or without , for the treatment of bacterial infections including respiratory, skin, bone, gynecologic, urinary tract, and intra-abdominal as well as septicemia and endocarditis."	"Cilastatin is a renal dehydropeptidase-I inhibitor. Since the antibiotic, imipenem, is hydrolyzed by dehydropeptidase-I, which resides in the brush border of the renal tubule, cilastatin is administered with imipenem to block the metabolism of imipenem."	"Cilastatin is plasma protein binding is reported to be 35-40%."	"Cilastatin is a chemical compound which inhibits the human enzyme dehydropeptidase. Renal Dehydropeptidase degrades the antibiotic. Cilastatin is therefore combined intravenously with imipenem in order to protect it from dehydropeptidase and prolong its antibacterial effect. However, cilastatin in and of itself does not have any antibacterial activity. The increased renal excretion of unchanged imipenem appears to prevent proximal tubular necrosis associated with high doses of imipenem."	"Cilastatin is a solid."	"Cilastatin is anatomically related to antiinfectives for systemic use."	"Cilastatin is in the therapeutic group of antibacterials for systemic use."	"Cilastatin is pharmacologically related to other beta-lactam antibacterials."	"The chemical and functional group of  is carbapenems."	"Cilastatin is part of Cycloparaffins ; Cyclopropanes ; Dipeptidase Inhibitors ; Enzyme Inhibitors ; OAT1/SLC22A6 inhibitors ; OAT3/SLC22A8 Inhibitors ; Protease Inhibitors ; Renal Dehydropeptidase Inhibitor."	"Cilastatin is approved and investigational."	""	"The molecular weight is 358.45."	"Cilastatin has a topological polar surface area of 129.72."	"The log p value of  is 0.47."
