19729	"Diosmin is a semisynthetic drug indicated for the treatment of venous disease. Diosmin is a flavone that can be found in the plant Teucrium gnaphalodes. Diosmin is available as a prescription medicine in several European countries, and is available as a nutritional supplement in the United States and the rest of Europe. It should be noted that clinical studies have been inconclusive and no articles have been published pertaining to its use in the treatment of vascular disease. When used in rats, diosmin has been effective at mitigating hyperglycaemia, and may also have antineurodegenerative properties."	""	""	""	""	""	"Diosmin is a solid."	"Diosmin is anatomically related to cardiovascular system."	"Diosmin is in the therapeutic group of vasoprotectives."	"Diosmin is pharmacologically related to capillary stabilizing agents."	"The chemical and functional group of  is bioflavonoids."	"Diosmin is part of Benzopyrans ; Capillary Stabilizing Agents ; Chromones ; Flavones ; Flavonoids ; Heterocyclic Compounds, Fused-Ring ; Pyrans ; Vasoprotectives."	"Diosmin is approved and investigational."	""	"The molecular weight is 608.55."	"Diosmin has a topological polar surface area of 234.29."	"The log p value of  is 0.23."
19730	"Indolesulfonic acid is a blue-colored dye used a marker in urological procedures, also known as _indigo carmine_."	"The half-life is 4-5 minutes post-injection "	"This drug was initially used as a kidney function test. The main application of indigo carmine at this time is localizing and visualizing ureteral orifices during cystoscopy and ureteral catheterization procedures. "	"Indigo carmine works as a dye that accumulates in crevices, cysts, and foveolae and stains the tissue blue."	""	"This drug dyes tissues blue, enabling easier visualization for accuracy during medical procedures."	"Indigotindisulfonic acid is a liquid."	"Indigotindisulfonic acid is anatomically related to various."	"Indigotindisulfonic acid is in the therapeutic group of diagnostic agents."	"Indigotindisulfonic acid is pharmacologically related to other diagnostic agents."	"The chemical and functional group of  is tests for renal function and ureteral injuries."	"Indigotindisulfonic acid is part of Coloring Agents ; Compounds used in a research, industrial, or household setting ; Diagnostic Agents ; Drugs that are Mainly Renally Excreted ; Heterocyclic Compounds, Fused-Ring ; Indoles ; Kidney Function ; Tests for Renal Function and Ureteral Injuries."	"Indigotindisulfonic acid is approved."	""	""	""	""
