20680	"Fenbufen is a non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug used primarily to treat inflammation in osteoarthritis, ankylosing spondylitis, and tendinitis. It can also be used to relieve backaches, sprains, and fractures. Fenbufen is available as a capsule or tablet sold with the brand names Cepal, Cinopal, Cybufen, Lederfen, and Reugast. Fenbufen acts by preventing cyclooxygenase from producing prostaglandins which can cause inflammation."	""	""	""	""	""	"Fenbufen is a solid."	"Fenbufen is anatomically related to musculo-skeletal system."	"Fenbufen is in the therapeutic group of antiinflammatory and antirheumatic products."	"Fenbufen is pharmacologically related to antiinflammatory and antirheumatic products, non-steroids."	"The chemical and functional group of  is propionic acid derivatives."	"Fenbufen is part of Acids, Carbocyclic ; Agents causing hyperkalemia ; Agents that produce hypertension ; Analgesics ; Analgesics, Non-Narcotic ; Anti-Inflammatory Agents ; Anti-Inflammatory Agents, Non-Steroidal ; Antiinflammatory and Antirheumatic Products ; Antiinflammatory and Antirheumatic Products, Non-Steroids ; Antirheumatic Agents ; Central Nervous System Agents ; Cyclooxygenase Inhibitors ; Enzyme Inhibitors ; Musculo-Skeletal System ; Nephrotoxic agents ; Non COX-2 selective NSAIDS ; Peripheral Nervous System Agents ; Propionates ; Sensory System Agents."	"Fenbufen is approved."	""	"The molecular weight is 254.28."	"Fenbufen has a topological polar surface area of 54.37."	"The log p value of  is 3.14."
