20902	"Hepatitis B Vaccine is an ingredient in the EMA-withdrawn product Quintanrix. It is marketed in Canada as Engerix B. It is also a part of Twinrix (Hep A/Hep B vaccine) available also in Canada."	"Evaluation of pharmacokinetic properties is not required for vaccines. "	"Active immunization against hepatitis B virus infection."	"ENGERIX®-B induces specific humoral antibodies against HBsAg (anti-HBs antibodies). It is generally accepted that an anti-HBs titre greater than 10 IU/L correlates with protection against hepatitis B virus infection. More than 90% of healthy adults, children and neonates developed protective anti-HBs titres one month after completing a"	"Evaluation of pharmacokinetic properties is not required for vaccines. "	"ENGERIX-B induces specific humoral antibodies against the surface antigen of hepatitis B virus (anti-HBs antibodies). An anti-HBs antibody titre above 10 IU/l correlates with protection to HBV infection."	""	""	""	""	""	"Hepatitis B Vaccine (Recombinant) is part of Actively Acquired Immunity ; Antigens ; Antigens, Viral ; Biological Factors ; Hepatitis Antigens ; Hepatitis B Antigens ; Hepatitis B Surface Antigens ; Hepatitis B Surface Antigens, drug effects ; Inactivated Hepatitis B Virus Vaccine ; Vaccines."	"Hepatitis B Vaccine (Recombinant) is approved and withdrawn."	""	""	""	""
