21204	"Oxaprotiline is a norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor of the tetracyclic antidepressant family that is related to maprotiline. This drug was never marketed. Oxaprotiline is a racemic mixture of the isomers levoprotiline and dextroprotiline. Levoprotiline is the R or levo isomer of oxaprotiline (CGP-12,103-A). Dextroprotiline is the S or dextro isomer of oxaprotiline (CGP-12,104-A). Both enantiomers have antidepressant effects but levoprotiline also is an antihistamine and dextroprotiline has many other pharmacological actions."	""	"Investigated for the treatment of depression."	""	""	""	"Oxaprotiline is a solid."	""	""	""	""	"Oxaprotiline is part of Agents that produce hypertension ; Agents that reduce seizure threshold ; Anthracenes ; Antidepressive Agents ; Antidepressive Agents, Tetracyclic ; Antidepressive Agents, Tricyclic ; Central Nervous System Agents ; Central Nervous System Depressants ; Neurotoxic agents ; Psychotropic Drugs ; Serotonergic Drugs Shown to Increase Risk of Serotonin Syndrome."	"Oxaprotiline is experimental."	""	""	""	""
