21521	"Ferric sulfate has the molecular formula of Fe2SO4, and it is a dark brown or yellow chemical agent with acidic properties. It is produced by the reaction of sulfuric acid and an oxidizing agent. It is used in different fields such as dermatology, dentistry and it is thought to present hemostatic properties by interacting chemically with blood proteins. By the FDA, ferric sulfate is a direct food substance affirmed in the GRAS category (Generally Recognized As Safe)."	"Pharmacokinetic studies related to the half-life of ferric sulfate have not been performed. "	"Ferric sulfate was first used in dermatology as part of the Monsel's solution. This solution is an antihemorrhagic agent used in skin and mucosal biopsies. The use of ferric sulfate in dermatology is under review as ferric sulfate is corrosive and injurious and it can cause degenerative changes that are not observed with other alternatives like collagen."	"The main function of ferric sulfate is as a hemostatic agent in different medical practices. This hemostatic function is achieved when ferric sulfate is applied directly in the damaged tissue. Once applied, ferric sulfate forms ferric ion-protein complex which helps the sealing of the damaged vessels mechanically. The formation of agglutinated protein complexes produces the generation of occlusion in the capillary orifices. The formation of the ferric protein complex is thought to be due to a chemical reaction between the acidic form of ferric sulfate and the blood proteins."	"Ferric sulfate presents very high protein binding properties, this property is thought to be due to its acidic profile."	"The administration of ferric sulfate as a dermatologic agent has showed delayed reepithelialization and dyspigmentation. Some studies have reported the generation of inflammation in the sites of administration of ferric sulfate."	"Ferric sulfate is a solid."	""	""	""	""	"Ferric sulfate is part of Hematinics ; Iron Compounds ; Organometallic Compounds ; Parenteral Iron Replacement ; Phosphate Binder."	"Ferric sulfate is approved."	""	"The molecular weight is 399.86."	"Ferric sulfate has a topological polar surface area of 80.26."	""
